Kernel_fallback
├── when the selector is onERC721Received
│   └── it should return the selector as magic value
├── when the selector is onERC1155Received
│   └── it should return the selector as magic value
├── when the selector is onERC1155BatchReceived
│   └── it should return the selector as magic value
└── when the selector is a custom registered selector
    ├── given the selector is not registered
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidSelector error
    ├── given the selector is registered but hook is address0
    │   ├── when the caller is not the EntryPoint
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidSelector error
    │   └── when the caller is the EntryPoint
    │       ├── given callType is CALL
    │       │   ├── it should call the target with msgdata plus msgsender
    │       │   ├── when the target call succeeds
    │       │   │   └── it should return the call result
    │       │   └── when the target call reverts
    │       │       └── it should propagate the revert
    │       ├── given callType is DELEGATECALL
    │       │   ├── it should delegatecall the target with msgdata
    │       │   ├── when the delegatecall succeeds
    │       │   │   └── it should return the delegatecall result
    │       │   └── when the delegatecall reverts
    │       │       └── it should propagate the revert
    │       └── given callType is unsupported
    │           └── it should revert with InvalidCallType error
    ├── given the selector is registered with hook set to address1
    │   ├── it should skip preHook and postHook
    │   ├── it should allow any caller
    │   ├── given callType is CALL
    │   │   ├── it should call the target with msgdata plus msgsender
    │   │   ├── when the target call succeeds
    │   │   │   └── it should return the call result
    │   │   └── when the target call reverts
    │   │       └── it should propagate the revert
    │   ├── given callType is DELEGATECALL
    │   │   ├── it should delegatecall the target with msgdata
    │   │   ├── when the delegatecall succeeds
    │   │   │   └── it should return the delegatecall result
    │   │   └── when the delegatecall reverts
    │   │       └── it should propagate the revert
    │   └── given callType is unsupported
    │       └── it should revert with InvalidCallType error
    └── given the selector is registered with a hook contract
        ├── it should call preHook on the hook with msgdata
        ├── given preHook reverts
        │   └── it should propagate the revert
        └── given preHook succeeds
            ├── given callType is CALL
            │   ├── it should call the target with msgdata plus msgsender
            │   ├── when the target call succeeds
            │   │   ├── it should call postHook with the context from preHook
            │   │   ├── given postHook reverts
            │   │   │   └── it should propagate the revert
            │   │   └── given postHook succeeds
            │   │       └── it should return the call result
            │   └── when the target call reverts
            │       └── it should propagate the revert and skip postHook
            ├── given callType is DELEGATECALL
            │   ├── it should delegatecall the target with msgdata
            │   ├── when the delegatecall succeeds
            │   │   ├── it should call postHook with the context from preHook
            │   │   ├── given postHook reverts
            │   │   │   └── it should propagate the revert
            │   │   └── given postHook succeeds
            │   │       └── it should return the delegatecall result
            │   └── when the delegatecall reverts
            │       └── it should propagate the revert and skip postHook
            └── given callType is unsupported
                └── it should revert with InvalidCallType error
